cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use mltpy in scientific work, please cite both the software and the underlying methodology (Hothorn 2020)."
title: "mltpy: Conditional Transformation Models in Python"
abstract: >-
  A Python port of the R mlt package for fitting Conditional
  Transformation Models. Estimates a monotone Bernstein-polynomial
  transformation h(y|x) by maximum likelihood, yielding CDFs,
  densities, quantiles, hazards, and samples from a single fitted
  object. Supports exact, right-, left-, and interval-censored data.
type: software
authors:
